# Module Menu i18n Conventions

Use when adding or updating module admin/settings menu contributions.

## Translation Scope

- **Module menu strings MUST live in the module.** Use the module's own i18n namespace and locale files (`ui/locales/en.json`, `ui/locales/de.json`), not app `common.json`.
- Do not add module menu keys (e.g. `menu.contacts`, `menu.projects`, `menu.invoices`) to `apps/ui/src/locales/*/common.json`.

## Namespaced labelKeys

- Use namespaced `labelKey` values for all `registerAdminMenuItem` and `registerSettingsItem` contributions.
- Format: `<namespace>:<key>` — e.g. `contacts:menu.contacts`, `projects:menu.projects`, `offers:menu.offers`, `invoices:menu`, `team:menu`.
- The namespace must match the module's registered i18n namespace in `ui/plugin.ts`.

## UI Plugin Example

```tsx
engenty.UI.registerAdminMenuItem({
  id: "my-module.menu",
  section: "modules",
  label: "My Module",
  labelKey: "my-module:menu",  // or "my-module:menu.myModule" for nested
  to: "/module/my-module",
  icon: Icon,
  order: 100,
});
```

## Module Locale Shape

- Add the corresponding keys to `ui/locales/en.json` and `ui/locales/de.json`.
- Use flat or nested keys as needed: `"menu": "My Module"` or `"menu": { "myModule": "My Module", "subItem": "Sub" }`.
- For breadcrumbs and pages, use the same keys from the module namespace: `t("menu")`, `t("menu.contacts")`, etc.

## App Preloading

- The app preloads namespaces from `labelKey` values (extracting the prefix before `:`) before building the sidebar. No extra wiring required.
